WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:06.470
At the height of Paris Hilton's powers, Hollywood&nbsp;
greenlit a film called "The Hottie and the&nbsp;Nottie." 

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:10.640
By the time the movie had been filmed and&nbsp;
dumped into theaters, it was already a punchline.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:15.140
It might just be one of the worst films&nbsp;
of all time. Hilton plays a "hottie"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:19.280
who refuses to date until her "nottie"&nbsp;
friend also finds somebody. In theory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.020
the film was a comedy — but ultimately,&nbsp;
its parade of mean-spirited characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.520
gross-out nonsense and offensive&nbsp;
plot points yielded negative laughs.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.540
Richard Roeper was particularly scathing&nbsp;
in his assessment of the actors, saying,

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.480
"Nobody in this movie should&nbsp;
really have a career in movies."

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.980
Joel David Moore, who played the film's male&nbsp;
lead Nate Cooper, won the Razzie award for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.720
worst onscreen couple along with Hilton. He&nbsp;
must be grateful that James Cameron didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.700
feel like Roeper did about his acting abilities,&nbsp;
casting him as Dr. Norm Spellman in "Avatar."

